Perform following SQL queries on the database SEIT 
I. Create table emp1 same emp. 
II. Add a column to the existing table EMP1 which will hold the grade for each employee.  
III. Delete the column grade from emp table.  
IV. Modify table EMP1 ADD CONSTRAINT EMPNO_P primary key on column empno.  
V. Delete the primary key constraint from emp table;  
VI. Modify table EMP1 ADD CONSTRAINT SAL_C check sal is greater than 100.  
VII. Modify table EMP1 modify data type of sal to int(14,2).  
VIII. Add constraint default on ename column of student table. 
IX. Delete constraint default on name column of student table. 
X. Modify table EMP1 drop column SAL. 


show databases; 
use seit26; 
drop table if exists emp1; 
create table emp1 as select * from emp; 
select * from emp1; 
alter table emp1 add grade varchar(10); 
select * from emp1; 
alter table emp1 drop column grade; 
select * from emp1; 
alter table emp1 add constraint empno_p primary key (empno); 
select * from emp1; 
alter table emp1 drop primary key; 
select * from emp1; 
alter table emp1 add constraint sal_c check (sal > 100); 
select * from emp1; 
alter table emp1 modify sal decimal(14,2); 
select * from emp1; 
alter table emp1 alter ename set default 'unknown'; 
select * from emp1; 
alter table emp1 alter ename drop default; 
select * from emp1; 
alter table emp1 drop column sal; 
